<!--
  Bangla translations of the user-facing labels Salah's calendar, Ramadan and navigation surfaces use.

  How these are selected: by the device's own locale, or by the language selector on
  Settings > General (see docs/LOCALIZATION.md). The selector stores its choice as a stable language
  identifier and the shell applies it to every screen without recreating the activity, so these strings
  are reached either way.

  This is a PARTIAL translation of the explanatory strings on purpose. Android falls back to
  values/strings.xml for anything not listed here, and Salah's English wording makes specific claims
  about sources and limits that must not be translated loosely — so the explanatory paragraphs that
  state what is estimated and what is not stay in English until someone competent to review that
  wording has reviewed it.

  The Calendar screen is the deliberate exception. Every string that screen shows is translated here,
  including its explanatory and error text, because it is the screen this phase localises in full and a
  half-Bengali calendar is exactly what a reader would notice first. The same goes for the language
  selector's own labels: a control that changes the interface language has to be legible in both.

  The calendar's date language (which script and numerals the dates themselves use) is a separate,
  explicit setting and is not affected by the interface language — see Calendar settings.
-->
